cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PRAXIS in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "PRAXIS: End-to-End AI Clinical Documentation for UK General Practice"
abstract: >-
  PRAXIS converts GP consultation audio into structured SOAP notes with SNOMED CT
  coding, safety-netting, and post-generation quality validation. It combines a
  custom Conformer-CTC ASR (PRAXIS-AUSCULT), an ECAPA-TDNN diariser (PRAXIS-TIMBRE),
  a QLoRA SOAP generator (PRAXIS-SOAP-v1), and a TrustScore verification stack.
  Developed as a University of Leicester MSc dissertation project (module MA7097).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Satyawan
    family-names: Singh
    affiliation: "University of Leicester"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
